[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575312296","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101201#issuecomment-2575312296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101201","id":2575312296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZgCWo","user":{"login":"Cere-dev","id":40390402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzkwNDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40390402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/Cere-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T13:36:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T13:36:53Z","body":"I'm almost sure that's because the engine/GDScript doesn't know yet the type of the Node you are referring to.\nIf you prepare the node beforehand it will autocomplete properly.\nTested with (using a Node3D I had in another project):\n```\nextends Node3D\n\n@onready var icon: Node2D = $icon\n\n# Called when the node enters the scene tree for the first time.\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar tw := create_tween()\n\ttw.tween_property(icon,\n```\n<img width=\"578\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/530c6325-a6ac-42f4-9914-430f88310060\" />\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575312296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575326265","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101201#issuecomment-2575326265","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101201","id":2575326265,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZgFw5","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T13:42:45Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T13:42:45Z","body":"Maybe it doesn't know the type, but it's able to show the list of properties. If it shows the list, the list should be usable.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575326265/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575382557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101201#issuecomment-2575382557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101201","id":2575382557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZgTgd","user":{"login":"Cere-dev","id":40390402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzkwNDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40390402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/Cere-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T14:09:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T14:11:40Z","body":"> Maybe it doesn't know the type, but it's able to show the list of properties. If it shows the list, the list should be usable.\n\nHow can show properties of something it still doesn't know what type is?\nAs the [docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#literals) says, the dollar sign is like `get_node`, and `get_node` still needs to specify which type of node it is (for example, when casting) if you want to edit any property of it.\nFrom the total respect! ✊","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575382557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575421460","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101201#issuecomment-2575421460","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101201","id":2575421460,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZgdAU","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T14:26:45Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T14:26:45Z","body":"On the video I attached you can see that the list of properties *does display*, you just can't filter it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575421460/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575508175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101201#issuecomment-2575508175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101201","id":2575508175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZgyLP","user":{"login":"Cere-dev","id":40390402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzkwNDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40390402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/Cere-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cere-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T14:58:12Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T15:45:32Z","body":"> On the video I attached you can see that the list of properties _does display_, you just can't filter it.\n\nYep, it displays `Node` class [properties](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_node.html#properties), not Node2D, as `get_node` expects to return a `Node`. It still doesn't know you are trying to tween a property of another type of Node. \nAs a guy who works daily basis with Python, this could be a expected behavior from GDScript. Forces to have a good praxis on how to reference the nodes in use to avoid reference or type issues.\nI'm taking a look into the code and check if there's something we can do to reference the object properties we pass at `tween_property`, as it expects a `NodePath` as param.\n\nEdit: I just saw you were the guy who help wrote the `tween_property` lol, I'm sorry if it annoyed you or something, just trying to help on the development.\n\nI'm looking at `gdscript_editor.cpp`, maybe the issue is [in these blocks of code when getting the object](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/modules/gdscript/gdscript_editor.cpp#L2861).\n\nEdit: Maybe it helps, i confirm `native_type` of tweened object is `Node` no matter what you put, unless you cast explicitly.\nbefore cast:\n<img width=\"448\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc9e664c-8fd5-4ca2-8257-3ec742938f36\" />\nafter cast:\n<img width=\"778\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aace6205-0db7-4af8-94a7-539b60353730\" />\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575508175/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578351881","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101201#issuecomment-2578351881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101201","id":2578351881,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZrocJ","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-08T18:31:03Z","updated_at":"2025-01-08T18:31:03Z","body":"Can reproduce. The problem doesn't really appear when using auto brace (or quotation) closing. When quotes are not auto closed this scenario produces an unclosed string which the parser will never leave since it will encounter EOF before a closing quotation mark. The completion context necessary for the list, only gets produced after the parameter is parsed which it never is in this case. We should probably look into phrase level recovery for the parser when doing autocompletion. There are some other issues that would benefit from this as well.\n\nVery dirty workaround, put this comment at the end of all your files:\n```gdscript\n#\"\n```\nWell I guess that's not really an option 😅 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578351881/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]